{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794531669893,"sessionID":"ses_e2d9479afffe1hhk77mYJ4dg2W","part":{"partID":"prt_1d26c36bc002UCvXbK4qUkZ4Xh","sessionID":"ses_e2d9479afffe1hhk77mYJ4dg2W","messageID":"msg_1d26c22d6001GOtoQQfIz3Qzo1","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2b0e139c3498e66","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md, lines 1-186\n1: ---\n2: title: sk-design Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n3: description: Stage-two router at the sk-design hub root. hub-router.json selects the workflow mode; this document maps a design intent to the exact mode-local leaf resources that mode should load, so a request loads what it needs rather than a directory.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"sk-design surface router\"\n6:   - \"design resource map\"\n7:   - \"design intent routing\"\n8: importance_tier: important\n9: contextType: implementation\n10: version: 3.0.0.0\n11: router_state: active\n12: skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # sk-design Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n16: \n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: `SKILL.md` picks the mode. This document picks what that mode loads.\n20: \n21: `hub-router.json` selects the workflow mode from a request. This router then maps the design intent\n22: inside that request to the exact mode-local resources worth loading, so a request pulls what it\n23: needs rather than a directory. Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves on disk and dual-reads to a\n24: canonical typed pair through `leaf-manifest.json`.\n25: \n26: An intent that matches nothing here is a gap to report, not a reason to load everything.\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 2. INTENT MODEL\n31: \n32: Three intents across three modes. The split is real rather than decorative: authoring a chart\n33: canvas, authoring a diagram canvas, and reading values back off a surface that already exists all\n34: load different things.\n35: \n36: | Intent | Mode | What the request is asking for |\n37: |--------|------|-------------------------------|\n38: | `CHART` | `sk-design-chart` | Author a data canvas: one file, one question a reader answers by looking |\n39: | `FLOWCHART` | `sk-design-diagram` | Author a process canvas, in markup or in text characters |\n40: | `EXTRACT` | `sk-design-md-generator` | Read values back off a surface that already exists |\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 3. MACHINE-READABLE ROUTER (replay / benchmark source)\n45: \n46: The single machine-readable projection of the intent model above.\n47: \n48: - The prose is the human-facing contract; this block is the byte-for-byte source the deterministic\n49:   router-replay parses.\n50: - Keep them in sync: when a map row changes above, update the matching `RESOURCE_MAP` entry here.\n51: - Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves on disk and is registered in `leaf-manifest.json`, so each\n52:   dual-reads to a canonical typed pair.\n53: \n54: ```python\n55: # No always-loaded preamble: a design request loads only the selected mode's\n56: # leaves, so the hub default route stays minimal and a no-match disambiguates\n57: # rather than pulling three modes' references into context.\n58: DEFAULT_RESOURCE = []\n59: \n60: INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n61:     \"CHART\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a chart\", \"make a chart\", \"chart this data\", \"chart the data\", \"plot the data\", \"plot this data\", \"standalone html chart\", \"chart catalog\", \"which chart type\", \"which chart should i use\", \"which chart fits\", \"what chart fits\", \"pick a chart\", \"choose a chart\", \"best chart for\", \"chart template\", \"chart color system\", \"chart colour system\", \"data visualization\", \"data visualisation\", \"data viz\", \"bar chart of\", \"line chart of\", \"scatter plot of\", \"treemap\", \"waterfall chart\", \"heat matrix\", \"heatmap\", \"heat map\", \"calendar heatmap\", \"box plot\", \"candlestick chart\", \"stacked area chart\", \"stacked bar chart\", \"grouped bar chart\", \"donut chart\", \"waffle chart\", \"histogram\", \"parallel coordinates\", \"measured site's look\", \"theme a chart\", \"theme this chart\", \"theme the chart\", \"bar chart\", \"line chart\", \"pie chart\", \"area chart\", \"scatter plot\", \"chart palette\", \"chart's palette\", \"restyle this chart\", \"restyle the chart\"]},\n62:     \"FLOWCHART\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"flowchart\", \"ascii\", \"text diagram\", \"text characters\", \"decision tree\", \"process diagram\", \"flow diagram\", \"diagram the\", \"as a diagram\", \"create diagram\", \"diagram\", \"architecture diagram\", \"sequence diagram\", \"er diagram\", \"entity relationship diagram\", \"data model diagram\", \"state machine diagram\", \"swimlane diagram\", \"swimlane\", \"venn diagram\", \"org chart\", \"quadrant diagram\", \"gantt chart\", \"radar chart\", \"high-level diagram\", \"medallion diagram\", \"data flow diagram\", \"draw.io\", \"drawio\", \"mermaid diagram\", \"redraw diagram\", \"self-contained html diagram\", \"editorial diagram\", \"create flowchart\", \"ascii flowchart\", \"workflow diagram\", \"decision branch\", \"parallel execution diagram\", \"approval loop diagram\", \"export diagram\", \"create:diagram\", \"/design:diagram\", \"theme diagram\", \"repaint diagram\", \"brand the diagram\", \"venn\", \"mermaid\"]},\n63:     \"EXTRACT\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"extract\", \"design.md\", \"style reference\", \"design tokens\", \"measure this surface\", \"from a url\", \"from a site\", \"css extraction\", \"validate design.md\", \"style guide from\", \"measure\", \"extract design tokens\", \"measure a surface\", \"extract css\", \"design tokens from a site\", \"style guide from a url\"]},\n64: }\n65: \n66: RESOURCE_MAP = {\n67:     \"CHART\": [\n68:         \"sk-design-chart/references/catalog.md\",\n69:         \"sk-design-chart/references/color-system.md\",\n70:         \"sk-design-chart/references/template-contract.md\"\n71:     ],\n72:     \"FLOWCHART\": [\n73:         \"sk-design-diagram/assets/ascii-patterns/simple-workflow.md\",\n74:         \"sk-design-diagram/assets/ascii-patterns/decision-tree-flow.md\"\n75:     ],\n76:     \"EXTRACT\": [\n77:         \"sk-design-md-generator/references/extraction-workflow.md\",\n78:         \"sk-design-md-generator/references/design-md-format.md\",\n79:         \"sk-design-md-generator/references/quality-checklist.md\",\n80:     ],\n81: }\n82: ```\n83: \n84: ---\n85: \n86: ## 4. HOW TO READ THIS\n87: \n88: - A mode is chosen by `hub-router.json`, not here. This document only answers what that mode loads.\n89: - One dominant intent routes to one mode's leaf set.\n90: - Two near-tied intents (within the ambiguity delta) route to both leaf sets; the union is deduped by\n91:   canonical pair and capped at the selected-map union limit. `CHART` and `FLOWCHART` are the pair most\n92:   likely to tie, because a request to visualise something rarely says which canvas it wants.\n93: - This map lists leaves, which is why no `SKILL.md` appears in it. A mode entry is loaded because the\n94:   registry named the mode, not from here.\n95: - Load what a row resolves and nothing more; a resource already in context is not re-read.\n96: - No keyword match is the hub's UNKNOWN fallback: report the gap and confirm the target mode before\n97:   loading anything.\n98: \n99: ---\n100: \n101: ## 5. MACHINE ROUTER\n102: \n103: The hub's detailed routing prose, moved here from `SKILL.md` so the skill body keeps only a short\n104: routing summary and a pointer to this file. It sits last, after the stage-two map above, and it declares\n105: no map of its own: the `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` block in section 3 stays the only replay source.\n106: \n107: > **Compiled routing (default-on, flag-gated, additive).** Resolve the mode via the compiled router contract first:\n108: >\n109: > node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-design --prompt \"<task>\"\n110: >\n111: > Follow the returned decision. A `route` names its targets, a `clarify` or `defer` asks for disambiguation, and a `reject` refuses. On a `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}` sentinel or any error, use the routing below. The front door self-gates on serving authority. Compiled routing is now the default for this hub. Set `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=0` to force legacy routing fleet-wide, the explicit kill-switch.\n112: \n113: ### Surface Router, per-intent leaf sets\n114: \n115: Stage 2 lives in section 3 of this file. It defines the three-intent leaf\n116: model (CHART, FLOWCHART, EXTRACT), the machine-readable `INTENT_SIGNALS` and\n117: `RESOURCE_MAP` block the deterministic router-replay parses, and the how-to-read rules: a dominant\n118: intent takes one leaf set, near-tied intents take a deduped union, and no keyword match is the hub's\n119: UNKNOWN fallback rather than a silent default. Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves on disk and\n120: dual-reads to a canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair through `leaf-manifest.json`.\n121: \n122: This router stays a separate document from `SKILL.md` on purpose; [the parent-skill reference](../sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md#why-the-leaf-router-stays-in-routermd) gives the reason once.\n123: \n124: ### The discriminator\n125: \n126: - **`workflowMode`** — the public mode key: `sk-design-md-generator`, `sk-design-chart`,\n127:   `sk-design-diagram`.\n128: - **`packetKind`** — `workflow` for all three. There is no surface axis on this hub.\n129: - **`backendKind`** — `surface-router` for the generator, which resolves leaves from a reference\n130:   set. `template-scaffold` for chart and diagram, which build an artifact from a form.\n131: \n132: ### Routing rule\n133: \n134: ```\n135: SKILL_ROOT  = path containing this ROUTER.md and its SKILL.md\n136: REGISTRY    = SKILL_ROOT / \"mode-registry.json\"\n137: HUB_ROUTER  = SKILL_ROOT / \"hub-router.json\"\n138: \n139: UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n140:     \"Confirm whether this measures an existing surface or builds a chart or diagram\",\n141:     \"A request to decide a value or review a screen belongs to sk-code, not this hub\",\n142:     \"For a measure request, provide the live URL or path; there is nothing to read without one\",\n143:     \"For a canvas request, state the question the artifact must answer, not the form you want\",\n144: ]\n145: \n146: def _guard_in_skill(relative_path):\n147:   resolved = (SKILL_ROOT / relative_path).resolve()\n148:   resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT)\n149:   if resolved.suffix.lower() not in {\".md\", \".json\", \".css\"}:\n150:     raise ValueError(\"only skill-local markdown/json/css router resources are routable\")\n151:   return resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix()\n152: \n153: def load_if_available(relative_path, seen):\n154:   guarded = _guard_in_skill(relative_path)\n155:   if guarded not in seen and (SKILL_ROOT / guarded).exists():\n156:     load(guarded)\n157:     seen.add(guarded)\n158:     return True\n159:   return False\n160: \n161: seen = set()\n162: if not REGISTRY.exists() or not HUB_ROUTER.exists():\n163:   return defer(\"router metadata missing; inspect sk-design/mode-registry.json and sk-design/hub-router.json\")\n164: \n165: read mode-registry.json and hub-router.json\n166: classify the request to one or more workflowMode values using hub-router.json\n167:   (dominant design intent; a command like /design:chart resolves directly)\n168: \n169: if two intents tie within routerPolicy.ambiguityDelta:\n170:   apply routerPolicy.tieBreak, then take the deduped union of their leaf sets\n171: \n172: if confidence is low or the intent is contradictory:\n173:   return UNKNOWN_FALLBACK with disambiguation_checklist = UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST\n174: \n175: for each resolved workflowMode:\n176:   entry = the matching mode-registry.json modes[] item\n177:   if entry is missing or entry.packetKind != \"workflow\":\n178:     return defer(\"unknown sk-design workflowMode; extend mode-registry.json and create the mode first\")\n179:   if not load_if_available(f\"{entry.packet}/SKILL.md\", seen):\n180:     return defer(\"registered mode SKILL.md is missing; repair the mode before routing\")\n181: \n182: return single or ambiguous according to hub-router.json routerPolicy.outcomes\n183: ```\n184: \n185: `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`: a design request with no clearer owner has no safe default\n186: among the three artifacts, so it defers and asks which one is wanted. The outcomes `routerPolicy.outcomes` defines are `single`, `orderedBundle`, `defer` and `none`.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md, lines 1-186\n1: ---\n2: title: sk-design Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n3: description: Stage-two router at the sk-design hub root. hub-router.json selects the workflow mode; this document maps a design intent to the exact mode-local leaf resources that mode should load, so a request loads what it needs rather than a directory.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"sk-design surface router\"\n6:   - \"design resource map\"\n7:   - \"design intent routing\"\n8: importance_tier: important\n9: contextType: implementation\n10: version: 3.0.0.0\n11: router_state: active\n12: skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # sk-design Surface Router — per-intent leaf sets\n16: \n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: `SKILL.md` picks the mode. This document picks what that mode loads.\n20: \n21: `hub-router.json` selects the workflow mode from a request. This router then maps the design intent\n22: inside that request to the exact mode-local resources worth loading, so a request pulls what it\n23: needs rather than a directory. Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves on disk and dual-reads to a\n24: canonical typed pair through `leaf-manifest.json`.\n25: \n26: An intent that matches nothing here is a gap to report, not a reason to load everything.\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 2. INTENT MODEL\n31: \n32: Three intents across three modes. The split is real rather than decorative: authoring a chart\n33: canvas, authoring a diagram canvas, and reading values back off a surface that already exists all\n34: load different things.\n35: \n36: | Intent | Mode | What the request is asking for |\n37: |--------|------|-------------------------------|\n38: | `CHART` | `sk-design-chart` | Author a data canvas: one file, one question a reader answers by looking |\n39: | `FLOWCHART` | `sk-design-diagram` | Author a process canvas, in markup or in text characters |\n40: | `EXTRACT` | `sk-design-md-generator` | Read values back off a surface that already exists |\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 3. MACHINE-READABLE ROUTER (replay / benchmark source)\n45: \n46: The single machine-readable projection of the intent model above.\n47: \n48: - The prose is the human-facing contract; this block is the byte-for-byte source the deterministic\n49:   router-replay parses.\n50: - Keep them in sync: when a map row changes above, update the matching `RESOURCE_MAP` entry here.\n51: - Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves on disk and is registered in `leaf-manifest.json`, so each\n52:   dual-reads to a canonical typed pair.\n53: \n54: ```python\n55: # No always-loaded preamble: a design request loads only the selected mode's\n56: # leaves, so the hub default route stays minimal and a no-match disambiguates\n57: # rather than pulling three modes' references into context.\n58: DEFAULT_RESOURCE = []\n59: \n60: INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n61:     \"CHART\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a chart\", \"make a chart\", \"chart this data\", \"chart the data\", \"plot the data\", \"plot this data\", \"standalone html chart\", \"chart catalog\", \"which chart type\", \"which chart should i use\", \"which chart fits\", \"what chart fits\", \"pick a chart\", \"choose a chart\", \"best chart for\", \"chart template\", \"chart color system\", \"chart colour system\", \"data visualization\", \"data visualisation\", \"data viz\", \"bar chart of\", \"line chart of\", \"scatter plot of\", \"treemap\", \"waterfall chart\", \"heat matrix\", \"heatmap\", \"heat map\", \"calendar heatmap\", \"box plot\", \"candlestick chart\", \"stacked area chart\", \"stacked bar chart\", \"grouped bar chart\", \"donut chart\", \"waffle chart\", \"histogram\", \"parallel coordinates\", \"measured site's look\", \"theme a chart\", \"theme this chart\", \"theme the chart\", \"bar chart\", \"line chart\", \"pie chart\", \"area chart\", \"scatter plot\", \"chart palette\", \"chart's palette\", \"restyle this chart\", \"restyle the chart\"]},\n62:     \"FLOWCHART\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"flowchart\", \"ascii\", \"text diagram\", \"text characters\", \"decision tree\", \"process diagram\", \"flow diagram\", \"diagram the\", \"as a diagram\", \"create diagram\", \"diagram\", \"architecture diagram\", \"sequence diagram\", \"er diagram\", \"entity relationship diagram\", \"data model diagram\", \"state machine diagram\", \"swimlane diagram\", \"swimlane\", \"venn diagram\", \"org chart\", \"quadrant diagram\", \"gantt chart\", \"radar chart\", \"high-level diagram\", \"medallion diagram\", \"data flow diagram\", \"draw.io\", \"drawio\", \"mermaid diagram\", \"redraw diagram\", \"self-contained html diagram\", \"editorial diagram\", \"create flowchart\", \"ascii flowchart\", \"workflow diagram\", \"decision branch\", \"parallel execution diagram\", \"approval loop diagram\", \"export diagram\", \"create:diagram\", \"/design:diagram\", \"theme diagram\", \"repaint diagram\", \"brand the diagram\", \"venn\", \"mermaid\"]},\n63:     \"EXTRACT\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"extract\", \"design.md\", \"style reference\", \"design tokens\", \"measure this surface\", \"from a url\", \"from a site\", \"css extraction\", \"validate design.md\", \"style guide from\", \"measure\", \"extract design tokens\", \"measure a surface\", \"extract css\", \"design tokens from a site\", \"style guide from a url\"]},\n64: }\n65: \n66: RESOURCE_MAP = {\n67:     \"CHART\": [\n68:         \"sk-design-chart/references/catalog.md\",\n69:         \"sk-design-chart/references/color-system.md\",\n70:         \"sk-design-chart/references/template-contract.md\"\n71:     ],\n72:     \"FLOWCHART\": [\n73:         \"sk-design-diagram/assets/ascii-patterns/simple-workflow.md\",\n74:         \"sk-design-diagram/assets/ascii-patterns/decision-tree-flow.md\"\n75:     ],\n76:     \"EXTRACT\": [\n77:         \"sk-design-md-generator/references/extraction-workflow.md\",\n78:         \"sk-design-md-generator/references/design-md-format.md\",\n79:         \"sk-design-md-generator/references/quality-checklist.md\",\n80:     ],\n81: }\n82: ```\n83: \n84: ---\n85: \n86: ## 4. HOW TO READ THIS\n87: \n88: - A mode is chosen by `hub-router.json`, not here. This document only answers what that mode loads.\n89: - One dominant intent routes to one mode's leaf set.\n90: - Two near-tied intents (within the ambiguity delta) route to both leaf sets; the union is deduped by\n91:   canonical pair and capped at the selected-map union limit. `CHART` and `FLOWCHART` are the pair most\n92:   likely to tie, because a request to visualise something rarely says which canvas it wants.\n93: - This map lists leaves, which is why no `SKILL.md` appears in it. A mode entry is loaded because the\n94:   registry named the mode, not from here.\n95: - Load what a row resolves and nothing more; a resource already in context is not re-read.\n96: - No keyword match is the hub's UNKNOWN fallback: report the gap and confirm the target mode before\n97:   loading anything.\n98: \n99: ---\n100: \n101: ## 5. MACHINE ROUTER\n102: \n103: The hub's detailed routing prose, moved here from `SKILL.md` so the skill body keeps only a short\n104: routing summary and a pointer to this file. It sits last, after the stage-two map above, and it declares\n105: no map of its own: the `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` block in section 3 stays the only replay source.\n106: \n107: > **Compiled routing (default-on, flag-gated, additive).** Resolve the mode via the compiled router contract first:\n108: >\n109: > node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-design --prompt \"<task>\"\n110: >\n111: > Follow the returned decision. A `route` names its targets, a `clarify` or `defer` asks for disambiguation, and a `reject` refuses. On a `{\"servingAuthority\":\"legacy\"}` sentinel or any error, use the routing below. The front door self-gates on serving authority. Compiled routing is now the default for this hub. Set `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING=0` to force legacy routing fleet-wide, the explicit kill-switch.\n112: \n113: ### Surface Router, per-intent leaf sets\n114: \n115: Stage 2 lives in section 3 of this file. It defines the three-intent leaf\n116: model (CHART, FLOWCHART, EXTRACT), the machine-readable `INTENT_SIGNALS` and\n117: `RESOURCE_MAP` block the deterministic router-replay parses, and the how-to-read rules: a dominant\n118: intent takes one leaf set, near-tied intents take a deduped union, and no keyword match is the hub's\n119: UNKNOWN fallback rather than a silent default. Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves on disk and\n120: dual-reads to a canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair through `leaf-manifest.json`.\n121: \n122: This router stays a separate document from `SKILL.md` on purpose; [the parent-skill reference](../sk-doc/sk-create-skill/references/parent-skill/parent-skills-nested-packets.md#why-the-leaf-router-stays-in-routermd) gives the reason once.\n123: \n124: ### The discriminator\n125: \n126: - **`workflowMode`** — the public mode key: `sk-design-md-generator`, `sk-design-chart`,\n127:   `sk-design-diagram`.\n128: - **`packetKind`** — `workflow` for all three. There is no surface axis on this hub.\n129: - **`backendKind`** — `surface-router` for the generator, which resolves leaves from a reference\n130:   set. `template-scaffold` for chart and diagram, which build an artifact from a form.\n131: \n132: ### Routing rule\n133: \n134: ```\n135: SKILL_ROOT  = path containing this ROUTER.md and its SKILL.md\n136: REGISTRY    = SKILL_ROOT / \"mode-registry.json\"\n137: HUB_ROUTER  = SKILL_ROOT / \"hub-router.json\"\n138: \n139: UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n140:     \"Confirm whether this measures an existing surface or builds a chart or diagram\",\n141:     \"A request to decide a value or review a screen belongs to sk-code, not this hub\",\n142:     \"For a measure request, provide the live URL or path; there is nothing to read without one\",\n143:     \"For a canvas request, state the question the artifact must answer, not the form you want\",\n144: ]\n145: \n146: def _guard_in_skill(relative_path):\n147:   resolved = (SKILL_ROOT / relative_path).resolve()\n148:   resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT)\n149:   if resolved.suffix.lower() not in {\".md\", \".json\", \".css\"}:\n150:     raise ValueError(\"only skill-local markdown/json/css router resources are routable\")\n151:   return resolved.relative_to(SKILL_ROOT).as_posix()\n152: \n153: def load_if_available(relative_path, seen):\n154:   guarded = _guard_in_skill(relative_path)\n155:   if guarded not in seen and (SKILL_ROOT / guarded).exists():\n156:     load(guarded)\n157:     seen.add(guarded)\n158:     return True\n159:   return False\n160: \n161: seen = set()\n162: if not REGISTRY.exists() or not HUB_ROUTER.exists():\n163:   return defer(\"router metadata missing; inspect sk-design/mode-registry.json and sk-design/hub-router.json\")\n164: \n165: read mode-registry.json and hub-router.json\n166: classify the request to one or more workflowMode values using hub-router.json\n167:   (dominant design intent; a command like /design:chart resolves directly)\n168: \n169: if two intents tie within routerPolicy.ambiguityDelta:\n170:   apply routerPolicy.tieBreak, then take the deduped union of their leaf sets\n171: \n172: if confidence is low or the intent is contradictory:\n173:   return UNKNOWN_FALLBACK with disambiguation_checklist = UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST\n174: \n175: for each resolved workflowMode:\n176:   entry = the matching mode-registry.json modes[] item\n177:   if entry is missing or entry.packetKind != \"workflow\":\n178:     return defer(\"unknown sk-design workflowMode; extend mode-registry.json and create the mode first\")\n179:   if not load_if_available(f\"{entry.packet}/SKILL.md\", seen):\n180:     return defer(\"registered mode SKILL.md is missing; repair the mode before routing\")\n181: \n182: return single or ambiguous according to hub-router.json routerPolicy.outcomes\n183: ```\n184: \n185: `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`: a design request with no clearer owner has no safe default\n186: among the three artifacts, so it defers and asks which one is wanted. The outcomes `routerPolicy.outcomes` defines are `single`, `orderedBundle`, `defer` and `none`."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794531669692,"end":1794531669893}}}}
