ng-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers && rg -n -A6 \\\"Command in the brief\\\" spec.md plan.md tasks.md | head -40\"},\"output\":\"tasks.md:54:- [ ] T003 Insert one line in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, right after the line `- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed`. The line is the exact content of `$S/bullet-draft.txt`: ``- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]` `` (`AGENTS.md`). Verify: `rg -c \\\"^- \\\\*\\\\*Command in the brief\\\\.\\\\*\\\\*\\\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, and `diff <(rg \\\"^- \\\\*\\\\*Command in the brief\\\" AGENTS.md) $S/bullet-draft.txt` prints nothing.\\ntasks.md:55:- [ ] T004 In `SYNC`, add a second block. Add the constants `START_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:start -->'`, `END_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:end -->'`, `GATE_TWO_CALL_MARKER = 'skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend'` and `GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'`. Read the first `AGENTS.md` line holding each marker, with a leading `2. ` stripped as `readGateOneLine` does. When both lines exist, write a block right after the Gate 1 block: the start marker, `## Gate 2 command routin...\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/logs/fanout-lineage.out:\n  Line 176: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794524202471,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O\",\"part\":{\"partID\":\"prt_1d1fa4176001yNk7MrWQWsvGpf\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1d1fa0d79001lwYAQaoL2oFJvR\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"id\":\"call_0fd93a5fd4e543a9903bb375\",\"tool\":\"shell\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"COMMAND:\\\\|Command in the brief\\\\|command registry\\\\|no command\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md | head -20; echo \\\"--- tasks 006 bullet\\\"; grep -n \\\"Command in the brief\\\" -A 6 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md | head -20\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"},\"output\":\"521:Correction first: I told you phase 003 (plain-chat command reach) was open only because of its holdout row. That was wrong. It has eight more unmet criteria, and I re-measured them today. Three are still fixable: one typed command (/create:agent) still ties with its own skill, four old spec-kit ids still sit in the Python compatibility list, and the prompt 'show me which packets mention the token cap' still reaches no command. Three are doctor rows whose phrases were reverted, where phase 004 now reaches 3 of 17 tune and 2 of 17 held-out doctor prompts with real embeddings. One is a one-time measurement-order miss. One asks you to judge that the doctor-only phrase gate was widened to every command. I recorded your holdout waiver and left the phase In Progress. How should phase 003 close?\\n--- tasks 006 bullet\\n54:- [ ] T003 Insert one line in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, right after the line `- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed`. The line is the exact content of `$S/bullet-draft.txt`: ``- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the ...","title":"gr