4: ---\\n15: \\n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\\n17: ## Task Notation\\n18: \\n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\\n20: |--------|---------|\\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\\n25: \\n26: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\\n27: \\n28: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise. `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `SSK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime`. `SYNC` is `$SSK/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-gate1-pointers.cjs`. `MAN` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agent...\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md:\n  Line 60: - [ ] T009 [P] Add one bullet as the last item of section 4, HOW TO READ THIS, in `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`: ``- A mode whose `mode-registry.json` row names a `command` has two whole entries: read that command's document in full and follow it under the policy the advisor names, or follow this mode's packet. Pick one and keep to it. A mode whose row has `command: null` has only its packet.`` (`.skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-doc/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-doc` exits 0.\n\n  Line 61: - [ ] T010 [P] Add the same bullet as T009 as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` (`.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-design` exits 0.\n\n  Line 62: - [ ] T011 [P] Add the T009 bullet as the last item of section 4 in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`, followed in the same bullet by: ``Where a mode packet names its command as its only entry, as `deep-research/SKILL.md` does, both entries lead to the command.`` (`.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md`). Verify: `rg -c \"has two whole entries\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/ROUTER.md` prints 1, and `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop` exits 0.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/acceptance-criteria.md:\n  Line 58: | AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given the three hub routers, When section 4 is read and the hub check runs, Then each holds one handoff bullet and each check exits 0 | `rg -c \"has two whole entries\"` prints 1 in each `ROUTER.md`, and `parent-skill-check.cjs` exits 0 for `sk-doc`, `sk-design` and `system-deep-loop` | Unmet | - |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/performance/logs/fanout-lineage.out:\n  Line 149: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794524016265,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O\",\"part\":{\"partID\":\"prt_1d1f76c9e001zUY02GqMDkHPg2\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2e0e4d38ffeP1JOC1np1mhw9O\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1d1f74cb1001TFaYpUS3hNXohG\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"id\":\"call_b379d8bf7fe14051b2386c93\",\"tool\":\"shell\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cd specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers && rg -n -A6 \\\"Command in the brief\\\" spec.md plan.md tasks.md | head -40\"},\"output\":\"tasks.md:54:- [ ] T003 Insert one line in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, right after the line `- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed`. The line is the exact content of `$S/bullet-draft.txt`: ``- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]` `` (`AGENTS.md`). Verify: `rg -c \\\"^- \\\\*\\\\*Command in the brief\\\\.\\\\*\\\\*\\\" AGENTS.md` prints 1, and `diff <(rg \\\"^- \\\\*\\\\*Command in the brief\\\" AGENTS.md) $S/bullet-draft.txt` prints nothing.\\ntasks.md:55:- [ ] T004 In `SYNC`, add a second block. Add the constants `START_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:start -->'`, `END_COMMAND = '<!-- spec-kit:gate2-command-pointer:end -->'`, `GATE_TWO_CALL_MARKER = 'skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend'` and `GATE_TWO_COMMAND_MARKER = '**Command in the brief.**'`. Read the first `AGENTS.md` line holding each marker, with a leading `2. ` stripped as `readGateOneLine` does. When both lines exist, write a block right after the Gate 1 block: the start marker, `## Gate 2 command routin...\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli/logs/fanout-lineage.out:\n  Line 176: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1794524202471,\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O\",\"part\":{\"partID\":\"prt_1d1fa4176001yNk7MrWQWsvGpf\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_e2e0e4b1affe2HORa6vu9VcI7O\",\"messageID\":\"msg_1d1fa0d79001lwYAQaoL2oFJvR\",\"type\":\"tool\",\"id\":\"call_0fd93a5fd4e543a9903bb375\",\"tool\":\"shell\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"COMMAND:\\\\|Command in the brief\\\\|command registry\\\\|no command\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md | head -20; echo \\\"--- tasks 006 bullet\\\"; grep -n \\\"Command in the brief\\\" -A 6 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers/tasks.md | head -20\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"},\"output\":\"521:Correction first: I told you phase 003 (plain-chat command reach) was open only because of its holdout row. That was wrong. It has eight more unmet criteria, and I re-measured them today. Three are still fixable: one typed command (/create:agent) still ties with its own skill, four old spec-kit ids still sit in the Python compatibility list, and the prompt 'show me which packets mention the token cap' still reaches no command. Three are doctor rows whose phrases were reverted, where phase 004 now reaches 3 of 17 tune and 2 of 17 held-out doctor prompts with real embeddings. One is a one-time measurement-order miss. One asks you to judge that the doctor-only phrase gate was widened to every command. I recorded your holdout waiver and left the phase In Progress. How should phase 003 close?\\n--- tasks 006 bullet\\n54:- [ ] T003 Insert one line in `AGENTS.md` Gate 2, right after the line `- Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed`. The line is the exact content of `$S/bullet-draft.txt`: ``- **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the ..."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"pattern\": \"two whole entries\", \"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794531680602,"end":1794531685726}}}}
